# Freedom Calculator needs no environment variables.
#
# There is nothing to copy and nothing to set. simulate.py reads two things: the
# config file you pass on the command line, and the flags you pass with it. It
# reads no environment variable at all.
#
# There is no API key, no model key, and no service credential, because there is
# no network call and no model anywhere in this project. The seed lives in your
# config file so a run stays reproducible from the config alone.
#
# This file exists only so the project matches the layout of the others in the
# volume. You can ignore it.
